<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - April 5.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - April 5.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended April 5</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   270	   0.55     484900  130.92   10.62</p>
<p>Reliance	     270	   0.46     355250   95.92    8.88</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   164	   0.33     528500   86.67   10.49</p>
<p>ITC		    375	   0.69     157800   59.18    9.59</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    210	   0.43     192100   40.34   10.68</p>
<p>Colgate		280	   0.56     138200   38.70   10.43</p>
<p>ACC		   1370	   2.70	22130   30.32   10.28</p>
<p>MTNL		   265	   0.44     113500   30.08    8.66</p>
<p>BSES		   215	   0.44     128650   27.66   10.67</p>
<p>Castrol		425	   0.90	63850   27.14   11.04</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 10.11 percent on an annualised basis in the carry forward account ended April 5.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
